  "report_period": "Week 24 (5th Jun to 12th Jun 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Alberta Shipmanagement have committed their Capesize \"Kerkis\" 176/2007 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 11/2026) to Chinese interests at USD 25,5 mill. Remind you that the two-years-older sister vessel \"Aliado\" 177/2005 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 07/2030, DD 09/2028) was sold back in March at USD 19,1 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Dimitris A\" 82/2008 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 08/2028, DD 09/2026) of Mykonos Shipping was committed to Chinese interests at USD 14,8 mill. By way of comparison, the sister vessel \"Mandy Morn\" 82/2008 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 10/2028, DD 07/2026) was sold a month ago at USD 14 mill. On the Supramax sector, following the sale of the \"West Bay\" 52/2004 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 02/2029, DD 08/2026, Scrubber fitted) in May at USD 9,9 mill, clients of Pacific Basin Shipping have now committed the sister vessel \"White Bay\" 52/2004 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 04/2029, DD 12/2026, Scrubber fitted) at USD 10 mill. In addition, Eastern Mediterranean Maritime committed their \"Poles\" 50/2002 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 11/2030, DD 11/2028) at USD 8,5 mill. Note that back in February, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Asian Pearl\" 50/2003 Kawasaki, Japan (SS/DD 03/2026) was sold at USD 7,7 mill. Interlink Maritime Corp have committed their Handysize \"Interlink Celerity\" & \"Interlink Solidity\" 40/2017 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 11/2027 & SS/DD 08/2027, Ice Class 1C) at USD 22 mill each, while the sister vessel \"Interlink Fortuity\" 40/2017 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 05/2027, Ice Class 1C) was sold a month ago at USD 21,7 mill.",
    "tankers": "The VLCC \"Maxim\" 397/2011 Shanghai, China (SS/DD 06/2026, Scrubber fitted) was committed to clients of Sinokor at USD 82 mill basis delivery Q1 2027. For reference, the sister vessel \"Kondor\" 296/2012 Shanghai, China (SS 04/2028, DD 04/2026, Scrubber fitted) was acquired by Sinokor in March at USD 78,4 mill. Latsco Shipping have committed their MR2 \"Hellas Fighter\" 50/2015 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 10/2030, DD 10/2028) to Greek interests at USD 39,2 mill. Remind you that back in March, the \"STI Black Hawk\" 50/2015 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 09/2030, DD 09/2028, Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 35 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route throughout Week 24 reported at low-mid USD 12.00's/low USD 13.00's fio level. Brazil / China rates were noticed ta USD 35.00 fio level, while Atlantic trips into Continent were fixed at high USD 15.00 fio level.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds with redelivery in the China and Singapore-Japan range were mainly reported between USD 18,250/24,250 pd. A number of Australian trips from China and South East Asia into Japan and South China were fixed at levels ranging from USD 22,000/27,000 pd. South East Asian trips to China and Japan were noticed fixed between USD 15,500/20,500 pd. US East Coast trips to East Med were reported at USD 32,000 pd and to Japan at 18,500/19,000 pd, while one voyage to Singapore-Japan was reported at USD 20,000 plus a ballast bonus of USD 1,000,000. On the period front, Kamsarmaxes were reported fixed between USD 19,000/22,500 pd for 11/13 months durations.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "South East Asia trips round trips were mainly reported at a range of USD 19,500/21,000 pd. Far East trips with redelivery to East Coast South America were fixed at USD 26,000 pd and to West Africa were reported on USD 23,000 pd. East Coast Indian trips into China were fixed at USD 17,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips into Japan were fixed at USD 12,000 pd. US Gulf trips into East Med remained firm and were reported at USD high 32,000 pd. On the period front, there was limited data reported, with a Supramax reported fixed at mid USD 22,000 pd for 4/6 months at charterers' option.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "East Coast South America trips into East Coast and West Coast South America were fixed at a range of USD 18,000/26,000 pd. US East Coast trips to Med were reported at USD 22,000 pd. Japan trips into South East Asia were reported at USD 14,000 and into China USD 14,500 pd. On the period front, Handysizes were reported fixed at USD 13,000 pd for 4/6 months."
    }
  },
